geometric-mean pooled p95 improves by at least 5%, at least one public native cell improves p95 by at least 10%, and no pooled cell p50 or p95 regresses by more than 5%. Retain every round, all negative cells and all resource measurements. A startup/ingestion/reingestion or RSS increase over 10% requires an explicit cause and review before accepting; never silently omit it.","query_order":"random.Random(31061 + 1009 * round + config_index), equal for paired engines","record":["every per-query sample and complete payload hash","MCP text and actual envelope hash","p50/p95/mean for every cell and every round, pooled and first/repeat rounds","initialization, fresh ingestion, unchanged reingestion","RSS/high-water RSS, logical and live DB/WAL/SHM size","indexed-content digest and source/cache/scope/budget invariants","both tokenizer counts computed outside timing"],"rounds":4},"guard":"The sole runtime candidate applies the envelope plus explicit FTS outer loop only when the project's inclusive rid span is at most half the full table's inclusive span. Otherwise keep the original statement. Read bounds through indexed MIN/MAX in the existing transaction; do not cache them. This structural guard was fixed after artificial tiny/interleaved diagnostics, before implementation or formal timing; it is not tuned on benchmark outcomes.","hypothesis":"For project-scoped queries, the existing pages_project index can cheaply supply a safe MIN(rid)/MAX(rid) envelope. FTS rowid bounds with an explicit FTS outer loop can skip unrelated postings while retaining the full project/chapter/session predicate before LIMIT, identical global BM25 statistics and deterministic ordering.","negative_diagnostics":"Unconditional range bounds slow projects interleaved across almost the entire table (about 18% SQL p50 in a 20,000-page artificial fixture), and range predicates without the explicit FTS outer loop can select a poor query plan. Those variants are rejected, not additional candidates."},"pre